# height: 14
# A context menu taller than the screen scrolls (Rust 1ef21198): the
# editor body's menu has more rows than a 14-row screen holds, so its
# bottom border says `↓`; the wheel over it moves the window a row per
# notch and the border says `↕`; End reaches the last row (`↑`).
#
# The wheel lands INSIDE a row, not on the box's left border: only the
# row is a `menu_item` hit, and a notch on the frame falls through to
# the editor underneath — which is exactly what this file used to do.
write a.txt "hello\n"
open a.txt
command view.toggle_tree
rightclick 20 5
expect screen contains "Cut"
expect screen contains "↓"
expect screen lacks "Save"
scroll 25 6 down
scroll 25 6 down
scroll 25 6 down
scroll 25 6 down
scroll 25 6 down
scroll 25 6 down
expect screen contains "↕"
expect screen lacks "Cut"
key end
expect screen contains "Save"
expect screen contains "↑"
key esc
expect screen lacks "Save"
